# Drop torque on both arms at once and refuse further commands.
#
# Served by the gate alone. The gate stops at once and asks the driver to let
# both arms go, asking again until the driver says it has; the answer here is
# that the gate has stopped, not that the arms are limp.
#
# The request carries nothing: there is one thing to do and no argument that
# could make it do less. Coming back is deliberate and takes the two calls it
# takes - SetTeleopMode to MODE_IDLE, then SetTorque - so that a single
# repeated call can never toggle the arms back on.
---
bool success
string message
